---
description: Protected branches, pull requests, and secret handling for this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

Promotion is `feature/*` → `develop` → `ppe` → `main`. `main` is the prod git branch and matches Databricks target `prod`. Cut work from `develop` on a `feature/<short-name>` branch. Do not force-push `develop`, `ppe`, or `main`.

Do not commit secrets. Credentials belong in Azure DevOps secret variables or a local `.env` file. `.env.example` lists names only. Do not read `.env`, `.pem`, or `.key` files into the chat.

CI and CD run only in Azure DevOps. `azure-pipelines.yml` is test-only. Do not add `databricks bundle deploy` to it. `azure-pipelines-cd.yml` is the only deploy pipeline, and it stays manual and gated. GitHub Actions under `.github/workflows/` stays disabled.
